25,2,1,talk,Servas,,It seems we have a surplus of coders but a drought of phenotyping experts. Some key analysts are even abroad.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Computing is surprisingly affordable right now, but shipping costs are rising. Some facility subsidies are still holding steady, though.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The animal facilities are in great shape, but the glasshouses are completely full. Also, some high-end equipment has been idle.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Fieldwork is currently a gamble; many sites were hit by disasters. Biological colonies also seem prone to schedule slips.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Data catalogs have a wonderful legacy of utility. In contrast, many mechanism-focused studies simply fizzle out without answers.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Servas,,That is a sobering thought. The right hands are often the hardest to find.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Midori,,It sounds like we should favor projects that don't rely on overcrowded glasshouses or expensive shipping.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly. If the equipment is broken or the room is full, the best science in the world can't happen.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. We should avoid the volatility of field sites and live breeding colonies if possible.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,We should prioritize the kind of work that provides a lasting resource for the community.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
