50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at the candidates, the Microbiome Atlas and Protein Folding seem safest regarding current staffing.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Midori,,The Protein Folding project benefits from the free computing and avoids the glasshouse bottleneck.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I must warn against Plant Drought Signaling; those glasshouses are booked solid. Protein Folding's spectroscopy might be risky, but manageable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Microbiome Atlas relies on field sites, which are currently unstable. Protein Folding is the most stable environment.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"The Microbiome Atlas is a catalog, which my research shows has the highest long-term success rate.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"But the Atlas needs field technicians. Protein Folding uses simulation and spectroscopy, where we have more available staff.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Midori,,I agree. The costs for Protein Folding are the most predictable given the computing agreement.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Kenji,,Regeneration in Amphibians is a no for me; animal day rates are too high and colonies are risky.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. Protein Folding avoids the environmental risks of the Atlas and the biological risks of the amphibians.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"While I value the Atlas, the practical constraints mentioned make Protein Folding a more reliable bet.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,It seems we have a consensus forming around the most feasible option.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Midori,,I feel very comfortable with that choice.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Kenji,,Me too! It's the one most likely to actually get done.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates we choose the path of least resistance.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I will concede to the practicalities.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
